// stage1-only: vec_with (ramfs.bastio reads table nodes in place)
// BastiOS kernel: boots, starts the shell as the first user process, and
// schedules processes round robin, preempting them on the timer.
//
// The kernel never touches memory through an address. Physical pages, page
// tables, CR3 and the CPU's user context are linear capabilities, and the
// Bastio prover checks every use of them before this file is compiled: a
// page is owned by exactly one table or by the allocator, a table is empty
// before it is freed, the address space in CR3 is never freed, and every
// buffer index and arithmetic step is in range.

